'''Wade Winston Wilson''' is a [[Mutants|mutant]] working as a mercenary. He left behind his vigilante identity of '''Deadpool''' behind to find a stable and fulfilling job as a civilian until he was taken from his reality and offered a place in the [[Sacred Timeline]] by [[Mr. Paradox]], a rogue [[Time Variance Authority]] agent and well as gaining a [[Deadpool Suit|new suit]] from the TVA. However, after learning that Paradox plotted to annihilate his [[Anchor Being Wolverine|home timeline]], Deadpool was sent to the [[Void]] alongside a [[Wolverine|Variant]] of his [[Wolverine/Anchor Being Wolverine|Wolverine]], with whom he formed a very uneasy alliance to escape. The two new friends were able to thwart Paradox's plans and kill [[Cassandra Nova]] before she could erase all timelines, and thus, Wilson invited Logan into his world and continued working for the TVA.

==Biography==
===Early Life===
====Becoming Deadpool====
{{Quote|You had a girlfriend?"<br>"Yeah, [[Vanessa Carlysle|Vanessa]], we met when she was a dancer.|[[Wolverine]] and Deadpool|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
Wade Wilson was born in [[Canada]] and served in the {{WPS|Special Forces}}, but eventually used his superior skills for killing to become a mercenary. Wilson then met and fell in love with [[Vanessa Carlysle]], but was later diagnosed with cancer, ending up abandoning her and seeking an experimental treatment run by [[Francis Freeman]] that resulted in his [[Mutants|mutation]]. This mutation gave him a regenerative healing factor, but also disfigured his entire body in the process. After these events occurred, Wilson then met and moved in with [[Blind Al]], as he was too ashamed of his appearance to return to Vanessa. In addition to that, he befriended a cab driver named [[Dopinder]] whom he offered guidance and advice. He then dedicated his time to hunting down Francis and demanding that he fix his face, now donning a red and black [[Deadpool Suit|suit]] and dubbing himself as Deadpool. Eventually Wilson finally worked up the courage to return to Carlysle despite his looks, but she had then been kidnapped by Francis now going as [[Ajax]] as a bait for Wilson. Deadpool was aided by [[X-Men/Anchor Being Wolverine|X-Men]] members [[Colossus]] and [[Negasonic Teenage Warhead]] in the fight against Ajax and was reunited with Carlysle. After killing Ajax, the two then continued their romantic relationship.{{Ref|DW}}

====Life as Deadpool====
{{Quote|I was... mainly I was team leader... founder, really, of {{WPS|X-Force#Film|X-Force}}.|Wade Wilson to [[Happy Hogan]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
Eventually [[Vanessa Carlysle]] was killed sometime later during an attack on Wilson by [[Sergei Valishnikov]]. In an attempt to move on, Wilson joined the [[X-Men/Anchor Being Wolverine|X-Men]] as a trainee, but dissagreed with their rules, so he decided to form the {{WPS|X-Force#Film|X-Force}}, which included characters [[Shatterstar]] and [[Peter Wisdom]]. However, on their first mission dealing with {{WPS|Cable (character)#Film|Cable}}, all of the members of X-Force besides {{WPS|Domino (character)#Film|Domino}} were killed while parachuting. Wilson ended up allying with Cable and was able to acquire his [[Time Travel|time travel]] [[Cable's Time-Travel Device|device]]. Wilson used the device to go back in time and save Carlysle from dying, as well as Wisdom and Shatterstar. In addition to this, Wilson also killed a [[Weapon XI|different version]] of him that was about to face off with [[Wolverine/Anchor Being Wolverine|Wolverine]]. Wilson then made another stop to a different universe and killed [[Ryan Reynolds]] as he read the script to ''{{WPS|Green Lantern (film)|Green Lantern}}'' before returning to his [[Anchor Being Wolverine|original universe]].{{Ref|DW}}

====Applying to the Avengers====
[[File:Wade and Happy.jpg|{{AltFloat}}|Wilson meets with [[Happy Hogan]]]]
{{Quote|I found my place, find your place.|[[Happy Hogan]] to Wade Wilson|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
On [[2018|March 14, 2018]], Wilson traveled to [[Sacred Timeline|Earth-616]] in hopes of becoming an [[Avengers|Avenger]]. He met with [[Happy Hogan]], telling him that he wanted to become a member of the team because he needed it. However, Hogan told him that the Avengers weren't members because they needed it, but because others needed them; Hogan ultimately turned Wilson down. Wilson then left the [[Sacred Timeline]] and returned to [[Anchor Being Wolverine|his universe]] dejected and depressed.{{Ref|DW}}

====Retired Mercenary====
{{Rewrite}}
{{Quote|I'm done, and I'm fine with being done.|Wade Wilson to [[Peter Wisdom]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
A depressed Wade Wilson broke [[Cable's Time-Travel Device]] shortly after returning to [[Anchor Being Wolverine|his timeline]], where his depression for being denied by the [[Avengers]] resulted in him breaking up with [[Vanessa Carlysle|Vanessa]] and eventually retiring from his mercenary life and gaining a job at [[Drive Max]] where his former teammate and best friend, [[Peter Wisdom]], worked.{{Ref|DW}}

===Normal Life===
====Celebrating his Birthday====
[[File:Wade and Peter Talk.jpg|{{AltFloat}}|Wilson assures [[Peter Wisdom|Wisdom]] he is done with being Deadpool]]
{{Quote|I'm happy. You know, that's because of each and every one of you. I guess what I'm trying to say is how proud I am, how grateful I am, to be standing in a room with every single person I love... I'm the luckiest man alive.|Wade Wilson|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
In 2024, Wilson tried to sell a {{WPS|Kia Carnival}} to the Chipman family. Because of his constant vulgarity, Wilson failed, [[Peter Wisdom|Wisdom]] reminding him of the possibility of continuing his heroics and showing him his [[Deadpool Suit|suit]] he keeps in his locker "just in case." Wilson quickly closed the locker and reassured him that he is done with being Deadpool.
[[File:Surprise Wade.jpg|{{AltFloat}}|Wilson arrives at his birthday party]]
That night, Wisdom insisted on Wilson going on a mission once a month, telling him to go all out while he is on what he calls his mid-life crisis like his friend once did. Wilson was distracted by construction workers taking photos of him by a subway entrance while Wisdom asked if he was grumpy because it is his birthday. The two eventually went upstairs to [[Wade Wilson's Apartment|Wilson's apartment]], where he is surprised by his friends that made him a birthday party. After taking a group picture, Wilson caught up with [[Dopinder]] and [[Shatterstar]]. He talked about ''{{WPS|The Great British Bake Off}}'' and how it prevented him from suicide with [[Colossus]]. He gave his opinions on abortion, religious freedom, animal and privacy rights, vaccines and global climate change, turning down [[Buck]]'s chance to give his as he doesn't have any speaking lines. He attempted to convince [[Negasonic Teenage Warhead]] that his toupee is a French hair system that [[Yukio]] complimented. He denied [[Blind Al]]'s request to use cocaine and restricted her mention of the drug and its synonyms per [[Kevin Feige]]'s request. Finally, he conversated with his ex-girlfriend [[Vanessa Carlysle|Vanessa]] about their living situations.
[[File:Deadpool & Wolverine Teaser Trailer (30).png|{{AltFloat}}|Wilson is taken by the [[Time Variance Authority]]]]
Everybody having sung "Happy Birthday" to Wilson around the cake, Wilson gave a speech about how grateful he was to have such a friend group, hearing a knock on the door as he blew out the candles. He opened it to a squad of [[TVA]] [[Minutemen]] whom he assumed were the dancers Dopinder ordered. Telling them that things were going to get sexual, especially when the Minutemen brought out their [[Time Stick|Time Sticks]], Wilson was grabbed in a chokehold by a Minuteman through a [[Timedoor]] behind him and his toupee was removed as was taken through it.{{Ref|DW}}

===[[Preservation of Earth-10005]]===
====An Offer====
[[File:Paradox & Wade at the TVA.jpg|{{AltFloat}}|Wilson is shown the [[Time Variance Authority Office]] by [[Mr. Paradox]]]]
{{Quote|I brought you here, Mr. Wilson, to tell you that you're special. In fact, you been choosing for a higher purpose unclear even to me. But one that could save the entire [[Sacred Timeline]] from a possible grisly fate sometime in the future which may very well need to be... [[Avengers|avenged]]."<br>"The [[Sacred Timeline]]? I assume I am going to... [[Marvel Cinematic Universe|Marvel]] at how... cinematic it feels? Gratuitous cameos? Indiscriminate used of [[Glossary#V|variants]]? The whole package?|[[Mr. Paradox]] and Wade Wilson|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
Wilson was brought to the [[Time Variance Authority Office]], where he awakened to [[Mr. Paradox]] in his office, Paradox being a [[TVA]] agent that explained to him that they are a "watchdog organization" in charge of defending the [[Sacred Timeline]]. Remarking the amounts of exposition for he gave for this [[Deadpool & Wolverine|threequel]], Wilson questioned if he was kidnapped as a consequence to his tampering of [[Earth-10005]]'s timeline with [[Cable's Time-Travel Device]]. Paradox denied it and asked Wilson to follow him to a computer room monitoring different points in the Sacred Timeline. Paradox further explained that Wilson was brought to the TVA for a higher purpose that would save the Sacred Timeline from a possible terrible fate in its future. Wilson was given the opportunity to join the [[Marvel Cinematic Universe]], thus finally meaning something, and excitedly dubbed himself "{{WPS|Marvel Entertainment|Marvel}} {{WPS|Jesus}}" before insulting {{WPS|20th Century Studios|20th Century Fox}}.
[[File:Deadpool (TVA).jpg|{{AltFloat}}|Deadpool wears his [[Deadpool Suit|new suit]]]]
Upon donning an [[Deadpool Suit|improved suit]] with [[adamantium]] [[Deadpool's Katanas|katanas]] tailored by a bearded man that often groped him, Deadpool came out of an elevator telling everybody to admire his suit, including [[Ralph (TVA)|Ralph]], of whom he was convinced he was attracted to him. When Deadpool requested to use Paradox's [[TemPad]] so he can let his friends in Earth-10005 know, he was told that he is not going back to his home universe, as there won't be one to go back to. Paradox showed him his timeline, receding and decaying due to the loss of the [[Wolverine/Anchor Being Wolverine|Wolverine]], the [[Glossary#A|Anchor Being]] of his world. He also told Wilson that he was tasked with overseeing said decay, which takes a couple millennia. Paradox thusly decided to accelerate the process with the [[Time Ripper]] as a compromise to the now overruled [[Reset Charge|pruning tactic]]. In response, Deadpool punched Paradox in the face, took his TemPad and teleported back to his universe during the 2030s.{{Ref|DW}}

====[[Battle at Logan's Grave|Fighting the TVA]]====
[[File:Deadpool & Wolverine Teaser Trailer (48).png|{{AltFloat}}|Deadpool arrives at [[Wolverine/Anchor Being Wolverine|Logan]]'s grave]]
{{Quote|I guess we're getting this team up after all.|Deadpool to [[Wolverine/Anchor Being Wolverine|Logan]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
While approaching [[Wolverine/Anchor Being Wolverine|Logan]]'s grave, Deadpool narrated how he never thought he'd be back again after the events that occurred behind the scenes regarding [[Walt Disney Studios]] and {{WPS|20th Century Studios|20th Century Fox}} and the rights issues, but he was mainly surprised because the studios wanted the "guy who shouldn't even have his own movie" back. Deadpool dug up Logan's grave, convinced he is not dead considering his regenerative healing factor and thusly not dishonoring his memory. He was enraged to find his skeleton, exclaiming the fact that his [[Anchor Being Wolverine|universe]] will end.
[[File:Deadpool & Wolverine TV Spot (7).png|{{AltFloat}}|Deadpool kisses a dead [[Time Variance Authority|TVA]] [[Minutemen|Minuteman]]]]
He sat by a log, conversating with the corpse, until [[TVA]] [[Minutemen]] appeared behind him. As they approached, Deadpool hid the corpse behind the log, halting the Minutemen. He refused to turn in his weapons, promising not to use them. Noting that the average human body contains 207 bones, Deadpool attacked the Minutemen with Logan's bones while dancing to the {{WPS|Bye Bye Bye|opening credits song}} of the film. He eventually came to use Logan's retractable bone claws, but had trouble using them, stabbing his own arm once and trying to fidget both claws out of one Minuteman's rectum and the other's crotch. Scolded for his actions by a Minuteman whom praised Logan for being the only thing worth something hailing from [[Canada]], Deadpool wielded his katana and simply bounced it onto the ground up through his face. He told him to keep his country's name, and his sword, out of his mouth before using the [[TemPad]] he stole to start looking for another Wolverine.{{Ref|DW}}

====[[Search for Wolverine|Multiversal Trip]]====
[[File:Deadpool approaches a shack.png|{{AltFloat}}|Deadpool approaches [[Old Man Logan]]]]
{{Quote|I gotta find me another Logan, a live one.|Deadpool|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
Deadpool kicked off his search in a universe where Wolverine is, "comic-accurately," short. Deadpool mocked the [[Glossary#V|Variant]] and left through a [[Timedoor]] upon his approach, starting a montage. Deadpool appeared in a city set ablaze, approaching [[Weapon X]], whom immediately attacked him. He met a gambling "[[Patch]]," whom clawed through his skull. He greeted [[Old Man Logan]], whom shot him in his torso. He plummeted into a place filled with bloody skulls, looking up to see a [[Crucified Wolverine]]. To his discomfort, Deadpool subsequently left to another universe, aweing at a [[Classic Suited Wolverine|Wolverine]]'s classic {{WPS|John Byrne (comics)|John Byrne}} [[Wolverine Suit|brown-and-tan suit]] before being knocked away by an alternate [[Hulk/Classic Suited Wolverine|Hulk]] whom prepared to fight Wolverine. He lastly arrived in a reality in which a Wolverine resembling actor [[Henry Cavill]] resided, revving up his motorbike. "[[Cavillrine]]," as Deadpool called him, was promised to be treated better than the "{{WPS|DC Entertainment|shit-fucks down the street}}." But Cavillrine simply punched him through a pillar while using his claws, and Deadpool teleported through another Timedoor.
[[File:Deadpool and Logan.jpg|{{AltFloat}}|Deadpool greets [[Wolverine|Logan]]]]
Deadpool fell into a bar, observing another [[Wolverine]] that looked "promising" even though he was drunk. Nearing this version of Logan, instructed to leave the bar, Deadpool insisted the bartender leave the bottle. He told Logan he must come with him because his [[Anchor Being Wolverine|world]] needed him. The bartender asking if they are going to fight or have sex, Deadpool turned to Wolverine, surprised he didn't react. With little time, Deadpool carried Logan upward, causing Logan to enable his claws, although they were remarkably short. Because he refused to come along, Deadpool pointed his gun at his forehead, Logan gulping down an entire bottle of beer despite that fact. He passed out, Deadpool dragging him and finding out he, after 20 years, finally has his [[Wolverine Suit|iconic suit]] on, much to his amusement.
[[File:Deadpool and Wolverine at the TVA.jpg|{{AltFloat}}|Deadpool threatens [[Mr. Paradox]] while [[Wolverine]] awakens]]
Deadpool arrived back at the [[Time Variance Authority Office]] with Wolverine, taking off his clothes so that the Wolverine suit is showing in full. [[Mr. Paradox]] scoffed at the thought of replacing an [[Glossary#A|Anchor Being]] and told him he selected the worst variant, the one who let down his entire world. Paradox repeating that there is no stopping the decay of Earth-10005, Deadpool commanded Paradox to call his boss and tell them that he denies the deal, only to hear a deafening silence in the room that made him deduce that the bosses are unaware of Mr. Paradox's sector's actions. Telling Paradox that he was going to tell them, Paradox pruned Deadpool and Wolverine, who tried to attack him.{{Ref|DW}}

====Sent to the Void====
{{Rewrite}}
[[File:Deadpool & Wolverine Trailer (36).png|{{AltFloat}}|Deadpool argues with [[Wolverine]]]]
{{Quote|I'm about to lose everything I've ever cared about."<br>"Not my fucking problem."<br>"Is that what you said when your world went to shit?"<br>"Come again?|Deadpool and [[Wolverine]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
Deadpool awakened in the [[Void]], a point at the end of time where all things pruned go, seeing [[Wolverine]] approach him. He insulted him in his request to help him stand up, prompting Wolverine to enable his claws, scaring Deadpool. He was stabbed and lifted upward, forced to answer where the two are. Deadpool says he doesn't know, but compared the place to the setting in {{WPS|Mad Max|''Mad Max'' franchise}}, though it would be IP infringement were that the case. Fed up with his humor, Wolverine stabbed his testicles, took a knee and injured his back with the other before pushing him off of it. Deadpool stood up, repeating [[Mr. Paradox|Paradox]]'s words despite Wolverine not caring. He then offended Wolverine by commenting on how he "let down his world" as per Paradox, being stabbed in the back when he looked away. Deadpool flipped to his back and slapped him to the floor, shooting his sides. Asking if he will be calm now, Wolverine answered by slamming the back of his head against Deadpool's and throwing him through the wall of an abandoned structure. Deadpool rolled against the late {{WPS|20th Century Studios|20th Century Fox}} logo, paying his respects to the former name of 20th Century Studios.
[[File:Deadpool & Wolverine Trailer (87).png|{{AltFloat}}|Deadpool fights [[Wolverine]]]]
Deadpool and Wolverine faced each other, Deadpool loading his gun magazines as Wolverine readied his claws. Telling the nerdy viewers to get their "special socks," Deadpool and Wolverine begin their duel. Deadpool fought Wolverine with his [[Deadpool's Katanas|katanas]] and "baby knife" against Wolverine's claws until his weapons are stuck inside of Wolverine's body. He was once again stabbed and almost decapitated. Deadpool stopped him by telling that he can make the [[TVA]] fix whatever happened in Wolverine's world. A cloaked figure called their attention. The man that Deadpool calls "The One" among other things told the two that "[[Cassandra Nova's Henchmen|they]]" are coming. The figure uncloaked himself after performing a superhero landing, confronting a group following a person named [[Cassandra Nova|Cassandra]]. Whom Deadpool thought was [[Hub:Steve Rogers|Captain America]] suddenly shouted the [[Human Torch]]'s catchphrase before attempting to attack [[Pyro]] using his flame powers. After watching Johnny Storm injure himself, Deadpool noticed [[Sabretooth]] catching Wolverine's eye. Deadpool paused the [[Deadpool & Wolverine|movie]] to tidy Wolverine up for a fight that fans have waited decades for, collecting his weapons and encouraging him to put up a good fight. Toying with Sabretooth's decapitated head in another ''Mad Max'' reference, Deadpool and Wolverine were eventually caught in a magnet, captured alongside Johnny Storm, and brought to [[Cassandra Nova's Compound]].{{Ref|DW}}

====[[Escape from Cassandra Nova's Compound]]====
{{Rewrite}}
[[File:Deadpool Wolverine.jpg|{{AltFloat}}|Deadpool and [[Wolverine]] meet [[Cassandra Nova]]]]{{Quote|If there's a chance [[Resistance|they]] know how to get out of [[Void|here]], we find [[Mr. Paradox|him]] and make those [[Time Variance Authority|TVA fuckers]] fix my shit like you fucking promised."<br>"I smell quest.|[[Wolverine]] and Deadpool|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
