[[File:Deadpool & Wolverine -BestFriendsDay (5).png|{{AltFloat}}|[[Logan]] and [[Wilson]] rest in [[Joe's Diner]]]]
Deadpool and Wolverine crash-landed upon a cliff, Deadpool lied on top of Wolverine, stating that he is almost done getting his knife out of his buttock. He vowed to tell [[Blake Lively]], about Wolverine's inappropriate thoughts. Wolverine instigated a new rule in which only he would speak from now on, Deadpool advising him that the rule is in the audience's disfavor. Wolverine created the plan of finding the [[Resistance]] Storm mentioned on the way to the compound and entered a pruned [[Joe's Diner]] with Deadpool. Wilson taking his mask off to eat spam, the spots of hair from his toupee were questioned, Wilson stating that nobody knew he was even wearing one. Logan was convinced that everybody surely did After his request to know what was "haunting" him was denied, Wilson reluctantly said that, in his world, [[Wolverine/Anchor Being Wolverine|Wolverine]] was "well-regarded." Wolverine responded that it's the opposite in his case. Deadpool could relate, being rejected by the [[Avengers]], the [[X-Men/Anchor Being Wolverine|X-Men]] and his now ex-girlfriend.
[[File:Wolverine, Dogpool & Wade Wilson.jpg|{{AltFloat}}|Deadpool holds [[Dogpool]]]]
Deadpool and Wolverine continued their travels, Deadpool informing Wolverine of how his Logan died while trying to save [[X-23]], Logan's genetically engineered daughter, reminding him of how [[Blind Al]] told him that pain teaches people who they are. After Wolverine remarked Blind Al's name, Deadpool detected a [[Dogs|dog]] running towards him in a little [[Deadpool Suit|Deadpool costume]]. He took off his mask to let Mary Puppins, A.K.A. [[Dogpool]], lick his face. A Deadpool [[Glossary#V|Variant]], who introduced himself as [[Nicepool]], ran after him and mentioned [[Ladypool]], remarking how she recently had a baby and can't even tell she did, which Wilson noted that might be offensive. Irritated by the answer why Nicepool doesn't wear a mask, it being because he has a gorgeous face unlike the other Variants, Wilson asked for a group of survivors of Alioth. Nicepool confirmed that they are out here, but that they shouldn't encounter a member of the hostile [[Deadpool Corps]]. Upon asking the location of the Borderlands, Nicepool offered them a {{WPS|Honda Odyssey (North America)|Honda Odyssey}} nicknamed the ''[[Ol' Betsy]]'' in which Deadpool couldn't take Mary Puppins, much to his disappointment.{{Ref|DW}}

