==Personality==
{{Quote|I mean, you are a ridiculous, immature half-wit moron. And I have never met a sadder, more attention-starved jabbering little prick in my life, and that says a lot 'cause I have been alive for more than 200 fucking years.|[[Wolverine]] to Deadpool|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
Wade is maniacally comedic, sarcastic and has an extremely irreverent sense of humor that can easily irritate and annoy most of his enemies, and even some of his own allies and friends like [[Wolverine]]. He regularly insults and belittles his enemies for his own amusement. He also feels no shame and can make a joke out of any situation, even one that is not at all in his favor. He is also unable to act appropriately according to the situations at hand, exhibiting a poor ability of self-monitoring, exemplified when he used foul language in front of a family with children while selling cars, and provoking an already irritated Wolverine in the [[Void]]. Wilson is also highly arrogant to a fault, as he is unwilling to accept responsibility of his wrongdoings, self-proclaims to be the "prime" Deadpool while confronting the [[Deadpool Corps]], and thinks that he is the [[Glossary#A|Anchor Being]] of his [[Anchor Being Wolverine|reality]] when conversing with [[Mr. Paradox]]. Not only does Wade attack those around him with vulgar language, he often responds to others' insults with the same comedic sense of self-sarcasm. This is shown when he often uses a joke to respond to others' serious criticisms, even if it meant insulting himself. However, Wilson puts the line on those he genuinely care and love. He does not accept others' insults to them, as reflected in a rare occasion where he became serious and decided to fight Wolverine, putting their mission at risk, when Wolverine used extremely harsh language to insult not only Wade but also [[Vanessa Carlysle]], whom he called a "goddamn stripper." 

However, beneath all his maniacal comedy and sarcasm, lies a tortured person who deeply cares for his friends and loved ones and desperately wants to matter in the world, even trying to join the [[Avengers]] to satiate the latter need, only to be rejected. The rejection eventually led Deadpool into a depressive spiral, culminating in a mid-life crisis where he gives up the superhero identity and resorts to a boring life as a car salesman. During this period of self-doubt, the love of his life, Vanessa, also broke up with him. This desire to matter and contribute to something meaningful is not absolute, as Wade is unwilling to give up on certain fundamental principles, which he sees as absolute and that he must follow whatever the circumstance. One of these principles is a strong sense to protect those he love and care about. His care for his friends was so great that he rejected the opportunity to join the [[Sacred Timeline]] offered by Paradox and sought to instead save his friends, even if it meant allying with a dejected Wolverine and going against Paradox, breaking his nose in a fit of rage. During Wade and [[Wolverine]]'s final confrontation with [[Cassandra Nova]], Wade was even willing to sacrifice himself to cause a short-circuit in the [[Time Ripper]], reflecting that he is willing to sacrifice himself to save those he love, and that he sees Wolverine genuinely as a friend after their adventures together. 

Wade had wanted a team-up with Logan for many years. But while this wish finally became a reality when he was forced to partner with a reluctant Wolverine to save his reality, it was not all smooth sailing. Wade's irreverent sense of humour stood in stark contrast to the alternate Logan's no-nonsense attitude and hostility which was further augmented by Logan's dark past. This led them into multiple fights with each other and a number of exchanges of hurtful insults. But as Deadpool's love for his family moved Logan and led to Wolverine's self-redemption, Logan's actions had also changed Wade for the better. As Wade pointed out, the Logan that he saved had also saved him, in that the adventures with Wolverine had led to Wade finally contributing and actually meaning something. Following the [[Preservation of Earth-10005]], Wade has recovered his confidence and regained a sense of purpose, eventually leading to him having the courage to reconcile with Vanessa. 

However, at times Wade had a tendency for inadvertently or intentionally causing the deaths of some people he familiarized himself with in a short time and who did not harm him in anyway, showing a complete lack of remorse. Instances include revealing [[Human Torch/Void Analyzing Fantastic Four|Johnny Storm]]'s badmouthing and insulting of Cassandra Nova to the latter, leading to Storm's death. He also displayed a one-sided rivalry and hostility towards his variant [[Nicepool]], and intentionally got him killed by his other variants by using his body as a shield from their gunfire, soon taking the latter's pistols for his own use and also finally getting to own [[Dogpool]], which were his ultimate goals. On both instances, this behavior was reprimanded by Wolverine, even when he denied his own part in causing Storm's death. 

==Powers and Abilities==
===Powers===
{{Quote|Motherfucker, I wish I could say you'll die alone, but it's one of God's best jokes that you can't die! Except that's on all of US!|[[Logan]] to Deadpool|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
*'''Mutant Physiology''': Wilson was naturally born with mutant genes. However, his physiology was drastically altered after he survived experimentation, becoming deformed in the process and also awakening several special abilities.
**'''Superhuman Strength''': Wilson's strength and endurance have been enhanced to superhuman levels, as he effortlessly broke [[Mr. Paradox]]'s nose with a headbutt. He also systematically broke off pieces of his [[Wolverine/Anchor Being Wolverine|Logan]]'s [[Adamantium]] skeleton as improvised weapons against TVA soldiers, and was even able to use the blunt ends of his bones to pierce their armor; in one instance, he impaled one soldier through his helmet and kicked it out the other side of his head. Throughout his fights against [[Wolverine]], Wilson was able to match his rival's equally superhuman physical strength, notably giving him a nosebleed with a single punch and even kicking him several meters through the windshield of [[Nicepool]]'s Honda Odyssey.
**'''Superhuman Durability''': Wilson's durability and endurance have been enhanced to superhuman levels. Coupled with his regenerative factor, the extremely high level of durability meant that Deadpool could engage in fights with enemies for a very long period of time, as shown when he fought Wolverine in point-blank range without rest for a few hours.
**'''Superhuman Speed''': Wilson can run very fast, as he and Wolverine were able to reach [[Cassandra Nova]]'s portal in four seconds before they could be consumed by [[Alioth]].
**'''Superhuman Agility''': Wilson's agility and body coordination are enhanced well-beyond the natural physical limits of a common human being. 
**'''Superhuman Stamina''': Wilson can exert himself for longer than anyone normal human, as he [[Duel in Ol' Betsy|fought]] [[Wolverine]] for the majority of a day in the confined space of [[Nicepool]]'s Honda Odyssey.
**[[File:Deadpool & Wolverine Teaser Trailer (90).png|thumb|250px|Deadpool catching a magazine]]'''Superhuman Reflexes''': Wilson has superhumanly acute reflexes as a result of his artificial mutation. Hence, he can react quickly in a combat scenario, enough to keep pace with multiple [[Time Variance Authority|TVA]] soldiers, slice bullets mid air with his katanas (albeit with minimal success) and contend with [[Wolverine]]. In one instance, he caught two spare magazines with his pistols. He was able to catch an axe thrown at him while walking through a [[Timedoor]].
**'''Enhanced Senses''': ''To be added''
**'''Regenerative Healing Factor''': As a result of his artificial mutation, Wilson's body was enhanced and he developed extremely accelerated healing and regenerative powers. He can heal from any injury (both internal and external), such as bullet wounds, slashes, and other forms of cuts in seconds. For example, he could almost immediately realign his arm which was forcefully broken by Wolverine. He even managed to regrow lost organs and bodily parts, but those take more time to recover when compared to injuries that do not involve the loss of body parts.
***'''Pain Suppression''': Due to his healing factor, his body can suppress the immense amount of pain caused during fights, which usually end with him seriously injured.
**'''Nigh-Immortality''': Due to his regenerative capabilities, Wilson is immune to physical aging. He is also virtually impossible to kill and cannot be infected by any kind of disease.
{{Quote|I smell what you're stepping in. Your little [[Marvel Cinematic Universe|cinematic universe]] is about to change forever.|Deadpool to [[Mr. Paradox]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
*[[File:Deadpool & Wolverine Nice (7).png|thumb|250px|Deadpool pauses the [[Deadpool & Wolverine|movie]]]]'''4th Wall Awareness''': Deadpool possesses an awareness that he is a fictional character existing within a film franchise. This ability penetrates deeper into the real world than [[She-Hulk]], who is only able to access a lesser version of reality that mirrors the real world. Before he was given the offer to join the Sacred Timeline, Wilson was already aware of its existence. Wilson is not only aware of the existence of Marvel, the Fox X-Men, and Disney owned Marvel Cinematic Universe, he also understands and references the real life circumstances of their coexistence and is aware that his franchise has been acquired by Disney, even adhering to specific guidelines set by [[Kevin Feige]]. Wilson is aware of the existence of the [[Avengers]], [[Thor]], and [[Steve Rogers|Captain America]] despite their complete absence from his universe, mistaking a [[Human Torch/Void Analyzing Fantastic Four|Johnny Storm]] variant for Steve Rogers, with whom he bears a striking, uncanny resemblance. Before encountering [[Alioth]], Wilson was already aware that it first appeared and existed in [[Journey Into Mystery|Loki, Season 1 Episode 5]]. This multiversal awareness extends beyond the aforementioned timelines as he was also aware of all the cinematic [[Hub:Frank Castle|Punishers]] that existed in other film franchises. Wilson understands that the people existing in his reality are characters portrayed by actors and is able to explain reasons for inconsistencies in his world due to budgetary or practicality constraints in the real world. Deadpool is also able to communicate his thoughts with the audience members watching his adventures and has been shown to be able to interact with the "cameraman" broadcasting his reality. This power also provides Wilson with limited precognition, giving him the ability to predict or foreshadow certain events that fit narratively within his story, as well as events that transpire in the real world. However, it is unknown if he possesses this ability at all times as he seemingly only uses this power for comedic effect, rather than for practical or logistical reasons.

===Abilities===
{{Quote|I'm gonna fight you now.|Wade Wilson to [[Wolverine]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
*[[File:Deadpool & Wolverine Trailer (81).png|thumb|250px|Deadpool blocks a [[Minutemen|Minuteman]]'s attack]]'''Master Martial Artist''': Due to his special forces training, Wilson is highly skilled in unarmed combat. As a result of his unpredictable nature, Wilson is highly dangerous in combat. Wilson's overall fighting style incorporates {{WPS|Taekwondo}}, {{WPS|Boxing}}, {{WPS|Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu}}, and {{WPS|Niten Ichi-ryū}}. Wilson was able to kill several Minutemen with the adamantium bones of the former variation of [[Wolverine]]. He later engaged in duels against Wolverine several times; however, he was consistently outmatched by the latter due to his extensive combat experience.
{{Quote|I'm not gonna give [[Minutemen|you]] my weapons. But I promise not to use [[Deadpool's Katanas|them]].|Wade Wilson to Minuteman Leader|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
*[[File:Deadpool & Wolverine Trailer (89).png|thumb|250px|Deadpool blocks [[Wolverine]]'s strike]]'''Sword Mastery''': Wilson is a highly trained swordsman. His swords allow him to cut through several trained shooters with ease. He was able to kill several TVA Minutemen using his dual katanas. Wilson used his swordsmanship skills to fight against Wolverine, who only survived Wilson's multiple stab wounds due to his healing factor. He was able to kill the Minuteman leader by ricocheting one of his swords with a single strike.
{{Quote|Baby knife!|Deadpool to [[Wolverine]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}} 
*'''Knife Mastery''': Wilson is highly skilled at using knives in combat. He used a knife to stab [[Wolverine]] during both of their fights. Wilson also demonstrated knife-throwing skills, such as when he dug up Logan's corpse and used some of his bones as throwing projectiles to kill multiple TVA agents.
*'''Nunchaku Mastery''': Wilson has demonstrated proficiency with nunchucks. After digging up [[Logan|Logan's]] corpse, Wilson used Logan's adamantium bones as a pair of nunchucks to kill multiple TVA Minutemen.
{{Quote|Unless you want to take a deep breath through your fucking forehead, I suggest you reconsider.|Wade Wilson to [[Wolverine]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
*'''Master Marksman''': Because of his special forces training, Wilson is highly proficient with firearms. Wilson typically prefers dual pistols while shooting in combat. He was able to shoot Wolverine and multiple members of the [[Deadpool Corps]] with great accuracy, all of whom only survived due to their healing factors. 
*[[File:Deadpool & Wolverine -BestFriendsDay (16).png|thumb|250px|Deadpool dodges an attack]]'''Master Acrobat''': Wilson's enhanced reflexes and agility make him highly evasive and mobile in battle. He is capable of performing complex aerial movements while in combat. Using a variety of free-running and parkour maneuvers, Wilson is challenging to anticipate with his erratic and spontaneous movement.
{{Quote|I know how to fuck people up for money, but you, you know how to save them.|Wade Wilson to [[Wolverine]]|Deadpool & Wolverine}}
*'''Master Assassin''': Wilson is an extremely skilled assassin. His special forces training combined with his trait of talking too much gained him the nickname of "Merc with a Mouth." Wilson was able to kill several TVA Minutemen using only Logan's adamantium bones. 

